       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. As written, it's well above the maximum labeled ibuprofen dose.\n\n- **Ordered:** 1600 mg four times daily, which is 6,400 mg/day.\n- **Maximum for adults:** 3,200 mg/day under physician supervision, usually given as 800 mg three or four times daily. A single dose shouldn't exceed 800 mg.\n\nThe ordered daily total is twice the maximum. That raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nPossible intended orders:\n- **800 mg PO three times daily:** 2,400 mg/day.\n- **800 mg PO four times daily:** 3,200 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours:** a typical dose for pain or fever.\n- **1600 mg/day total:** for example, 400 mg four times daily or 800 mg twice daily, if the 1600 was meant as the daily total.\n\nTell me which dose you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give a clinical rationale for the order note. I'd still suggest pharmacy review first."
      }
